From 6bdc54ae4004e94865037202aad360d5a4013321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:51:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mobile): pay via a Custom Tab instead of the app's own
 WebView, so UPI works
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UPI never showed as a payment option in the native SmartAppt Gold app
(Capacitor/Android), only on the web build, even though both use the exact
same Razorpay integration with no method restrictions configured anywhere.
The difference is the container: the native app runs its whole UI inside
an embedded Android WebView, which carries a "; wv" marker identifying it
as embedded rather than a standalone browser. Razorpay (and the UPI apps
themselves) treat that marker as untrustworthy for UPI specifically, since
completing a UPI payment means handing off to a banking app and getting
control back reliably — something an embedded WebView can't always
guarantee — so UPI gets suppressed while Cards/EMI/Netbanking/Wallet,
which don't need that hand-off, are unaffected.

Fix: for native only, open the existing web checkout page
(PaymentPage.tsx, already used by the plain web build) in a real Chrome
Custom Tab / SFSafariViewController via @capacitor/browser, instead of
Razorpay's inline checkout.js modal inside the app's own WebView. A real
browser context resolves the trust issue directly.

- hooks/useRazorpay.ts: on Capacitor.isNativePlatform(), hand off to a new
  /dues/pay-native/:billId Custom Tab instead of loading checkout.js
  in-page. Since that's a separate browser process with no access to this
  app's Redux/session storage, the current access token is passed once via
  the URL. There's no way to learn the outcome back in the app's own JS,
  so on return (Browser's `browserFinished` event) it just invalidates the
  Bill/Payment RTK Query tags and lets the bill's real status (paid,
  partial, still unpaid) speak for itself, via a new onReturn callback.
- App.tsx: added /dues/pay-native/:billId as a sibling of the existing
  /dues/pay/:billId, deliberately without the RoleRoute guard — a fresh
  Custom Tab session has no state.auth.user yet, which would otherwise
  bounce straight to /login. The backend still enforces that the bill
  belongs to the token's own user; this route is a UX convenience, not the
  security boundary.
- pages/dues/PaymentPage.tsx: now accepts an access token via ?token= (for
  the native handoff only — a normal web visit is unaffected), and skips
  the full app chrome in favor of a plain centered card, since there's no
  real logged-in session to build a nav around. Also now calls
  verifyPayment on success, closing a pre-existing gap where this page
  relied solely on the (now newly wired-up) webhook to ever record the
  payment.
- pages/dues/MyBillsPage.tsx: added a neutral "checking payment status"
  toast on return from the native flow, ahead of the actual refetch.
- Added @capacitor/browser (matching the other @capacitor/* packages
  already pinned to ^6.0.0).

Requires a new app build to reach devices — this is native app code, not
something a backend/web deploy picks up. Needs frontend/.env.mobile
(gitignored, not included in this patch) with:
  VITE_API_URL=https://smart-appt-app-development.up.railway.app/api/v1
  VITE_WEB_APP_URL=https://smartapptgold.integratatech.ai
before running npm run build:mobile && npx cap sync android.

